IMPORTANT NOTICE: Arlington County requires all applicants to thoroughly complete each section of the application, including prior job responsibilities, duties, and supplemental questions. While you may attach a resume, it will not replace a completed application. Incomplete applications will not be considered.
 The Department of Parks & Recreation (DPR) is seeking temporary, part-time TEAM Student Assistants to join our team! Through the Teen Entrepreneurship Amusement Management (TEAM) Program, students help bring community events to life across Arlington while building leadership, communication, teamwork, problem-solving, and customer service skills. Student Assistants receive on-the-job training and mentorship as they set up and run event attractions such as moon bounces, games, face painting, and concessions.
Major Job Duties: 
 Delivering and setting up moon bounces, games, and other event equipment;
 Supervising moon bounces and other attractions during events;
 Providing face painting and balloon art for event guests;
 Staffing concession stands and handling sales;
 Leading or assisting with planning and conducting recreation programs and events;
 Leading or assisting with recreational activities;
 Assisting with participant and program evaluations;
 Supporting participants of all abilities, including individuals with disabilities;
 Providing friendly customer service to children, families, and community members; and
 Performing other duties as assigned.
